Lavender bush
Approximate sizes:height - 420mm; diameter - 270mm.
In the archive:

  - * .max in version 2014, for rendering Corona 1.7;

  - * .max in version 2017, for rendering Corona 1.7;

  - * .mat library of materials for rendering Corona 1.7;

  - * .max in version 2014, for rendering Vray 3.60.03;

  - * .max in version 2017, for rendering Vray 3.60.03;

  - * .mat material library for rendering Vray 3.60.03;

  - * .obj;

  - *.fbx;

  - Textures.

All materials and model elements have logical names
The creation used Vray 3.60.03 and Corona 1.7Who works in the V-Ray version is lower than 3.1. Be careful, the materials in the BRDF section are Microfaset GTR (GGX), if your version is older than 3.1, then the BRDF field will be empty. Choose Blinn, Phong or Ward - which is preferable for you.For Corona render, it is recommended to put version no lower than 1.5, since the glossiness of materials is adjusted to the PBR.

Field poppy
The set consists of three models of bushes with different numbers of stems, different numbers of blossoming flowers, unopened buds and heads with fallen petals.
All objects and materials have logical names.The file was created in 3D Max 2017 for Corona render 2.0 and Vray 4.10.02 separately.Materials for Corona and Vray are in the scene, and applied to the boxes, from which they can be taken with a special tool.
Polycount scene 605852.
In the archive:

  - * .max file in version 2014 for Vray and Corona;

  - * .max file in version 2017 for Vray and Corona;

  - file * .obj;

  - file * .fbx;

  - textures;

  - library of materials.

The Vray materials are in scene applied to boxes. You can change the materials from Corona to Vray by using the pipette. All objects and materials in the scene have logical names in Latin letters. Complex objects have Unwrap. The file was created in 3D Max 2017 for the visualization of Corona and Vray separately, manually.
Who works in the V-Ray version lower than 3.1, be careful, in the materials in the BRDF section there is Microfaset GTR (GGX), if your version is older than 3.1, then the BRDF field will be empty. Choose Blinn, Phong or Ward - which is preferable for you.For Corona render, it is recommended to install a version of at least 1.5, since the glossiness of materials is configured with PBR in mind.

Game-ready rocks package for your next game project
1. Models
- SM_Rock_01;
    - SM_Rock_02;    - SM_Rock_03;    -  SM_Rock_04;
    - SM_Rock_05;
Textures
- Base Color texture map (.png);    - Normal texture map (.png);    - Ambient Occlusion texture map (.png);    - Roughness texture map (.png);    - ARM (AO, Roughness and Metallic) texture map (.png);
All the PBR texture maps are in 4096x4096 resolution.
3. Work Files
- Blender work file with all the rocks.
If you have any questions, feel free to contact me anytime. Cheers!

